Re: Implement saveAsTextFile() in the RDD class <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/browse/SPARKR-144>

Ryan Hafen <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=rhafen> Thanks for your comment. As Sun Rui <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sunrui> said, making `saveAsTextFile` mimic the Spark function was the goal of this PR.
Regarding the `saveAsObjectFile`, there are a couple of ways we could go about implementing this

1. I think your point about supporting a sequenceFile would be good to have, but it is tricky as full support for sequence file requires being able to serialize and deserialize Hadoop writable types (this should soon be possible if we better conversions from R types to Java types as described in SPARKR-145 <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/browse/SPARKR-145>)

2. However, I think your use case doesn't really require general purpose sequenceFile from what I can see. The RRDDs we have in SparkR are already serialized using R's serializer and saved as Array[Byte] on Java side. It should be pretty simple to save out these Array[Byte] as object files and then support loading them back in using SparkR. Let me know if this will work for your use case and I'll add some more implementation details to SPARKR-146 <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/browse/SPARKR-146>

