Re: Develop a serializer&deserializer for R objects in JVM <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/browse/SPARKR-145>

Thanks Sun Rui <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sunrui> for opening this issue. I think this is a good idea and something that will be useful across multiple efforts at integration (MLLib, SparkSQL, ML Pipelines etc.) In fact I would actually suggest addressing this issue first instead of using JRI (that adds another dependency which I'd like to avoid if possible).

Note that we already have some routines which we use to communicate between Java and R in serialize.R  <https://github.com/amplab-extras/SparkR-pkg/blob/master/pkg/inst/worker/serialize.R#L39> Right now, this includes functions to read, write integers and strings (on the Java side we just use DataInputStream/DataOutputStream in RRDD.scala  <https://github.com/amplab-extras/SparkR-pkg/blob/master/pkg/src/src/main/scala/edu/berkeley/cs/amplab/sparkr/RRDD.scala#L63> )

The next steps I see for this JIRA are:
1. Pull out the serialize, deserialize functions we have into a separate module.
2. Implement serializers, deserializers for numeric (doubles) and arrays of primitive types.

