> >> ~/rJava_0.9-6.tar.gz
> >>
> >> cd /root
> >> git clone https://github.com/amplab-extras/SparkR-pkg.git
> >> cd SparkR-pkg
> >> ./install-dev.sh
> >> /root/spark-ec2/copy-dir /root/SparkR-pkg
> >>
> >>
> >> Now when I try to do the R CMD javareconf step, I'm having an issue with
> >> setting the path to libjvm.so (see log info  below). I can muck around with
> >> environment variables but thought I'd see if anyone else had had this
> >> problem before I hacked together my own fix. This issue is happening either
> >> if I start the EC2 cluster using spark-ec2 from Spark 1.1.0 or Spark 1.1.1.
> >> It's particularly odd that this happens when I use Spark 1.1.0 as I don't
> >> see what would have changed relative to a few weeks ago...
> >>
> >> root@ip-10-225-159-177 bin]$ R CMD javareconf
> >> Java interpreter : /usr/lib/jvm/java-1.7.0/jre/bin/java
> >> Java version     : 1.7.0_71
